/*
Detection Rule: AWS IAM Access Key Used from New Geolocation
Author: Bryan Jorge
MITRE ATT&CK: T1078.004 - Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts
Severity: High
Description: Detects when an IAM access key authenticates from a country not
observed in a 30-day baseline for that principal. Attackers who steal access
keys frequently operate from different geolocations than the legitimate owner.
High-confidence signal when combined with sensitive API actions (AssumeRole,
GetSecretValue, CreateUser) performed during the anomalous session.
*/

index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
    (eventSource="signin.amazonaws.com" OR eventSource="sts.amazonaws.com")
    (errorCode="" OR errorCode="Success")

| eval principal=coalesce(userIdentity.userName, userIdentity.principalId)
| eval current_country=geoip(sourceIPAddress, "country")

/* Build 30-day baseline of observed countries per principal */
| appendcols
    [search index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail" earliest=-30d@d latest=-1h
        (eventSource="signin.amazonaws.com" OR eventSource="sts.amazonaws.com")
        (errorCode="" OR errorCode="Success")
    | eval principal=coalesce(userIdentity.userName, userIdentity.principalId)
    | eval hist_country=geoip(sourceIPAddress, "country")
    | stats values(hist_country) AS known_countries by principal]

/* Flag access from countries outside the 30-day baseline */
| where NOT match(known_countries, current_country)
| where isnotnull(current_country) AND current_country!="unknown"

/* Score based on what API actions were performed from the new location */
| eval risk_score=0
| eval risk_score=if(match(eventName,
    "AssumeRole|CreateUser|AttachUserPolicy|PutUserPolicy"),  risk_score+50, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(eventName,
    "GetSecretValue|GetParameter|ListBuckets"),               risk_score+30, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(eventName,
    "DescribeInstances|ListRoles|ListUsers"),                 risk_score+15, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(risk_score=0,                           risk_score+10, risk_score)

| stats
    count                   AS event_count,
    values(sourceIPAddress) AS source_ips,
    values(eventName)       AS api_actions,
    values(awsRegion)       AS regions,
    min(_time)              AS first_seen,
    max(_time)              AS last_seen
    by principal, current_country, known_countries, risk_score

| eval alert_title="IAM Access Key Used from New Geolocation: " . principal
| table _time, alert_title, principal, current_country, known_countries,
        source_ips, api_actions, regions, event_count, risk_score, first_seen, last_seen
| sort -risk_score

/*
TUNING PARAMETERS:
- Baseline window: Change earliest=-30d to earlier (e.g., -60d) for new accounts
  or accounts with infrequent access patterns
- risk_score threshold: Add | where risk_score >= 30 to suppress low-signal logins
- Whitelist examples:
  | where NOT match(principal, "svc-|automation-|pipeline-|github-actions")
  | where NOT match(current_country, "US|GB|DE|CA")

FALSE POSITIVES:
- Developers or admins traveling internationally on business
- Cloud accounts accessed via corporate VPN with exit nodes in multiple countries
- Automated pipelines (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI) running from cloud-hosted runners
  in different regions

RECOMMENDED RESPONSE:
1. Confirm the principal identity — is this a human user or a service account?
2. Contact the user or team to verify if travel or VPN change explains the new location
3. Review all API actions taken during the anomalous session for sensitive operations
4. If confirmed malicious: disable the access key immediately via IAM console
5. Rotate all access keys for the affected principal and revoke active STS sessions
6. Audit Secrets Manager, Parameter Store, and IAM for any changes made during session

INVESTIGATION QUERIES:
- Full session activity: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  userIdentity.userName=<principal> earliest=-24h | table _time, eventName, sourceIPAddress, requestParameters
- Sensitive API actions: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  userIdentity.userName=<principal> eventName IN ("GetSecretValue","CreateUser","AttachUserPolicy")
  | table _time, eventName, sourceIPAddress, requestParameters
- IP reputation check: | makeresults | eval ip="<source_ip>" | iplocation ip
  | table Country, Region, City, lat, lon

DATA SOURCES REQUIRED:
- AWS CloudTrail (management events) — enabled in all active regions
- Splunk geoip lookup or Maxmind GeoIP database for country resolution

PREVENTION MEASURES:
- Apply IAM condition keys (aws:SourceIp) to restrict API access to corporate IP ranges
- Enforce MFA for all IAM user console logins
- Enable AWS GuardDuty: UnauthorizedAccess:IAMUser/ConsoleLoginSuccess.B finding

RELATED TECHNIQUES:
- T1078 - Valid Accounts (parent technique)
- T1539 - Steal Web Session Cookie
- T1552.005 - Unsecured Credentials: Cloud Instance Metadata API

CHANGELOG:
v1.0 (2026-02-17): Initial release
*/
